draft: true
title: "USB HDC GUI test closure must separate render, window, and graphics capabilities"
category: platform-validation
trigger: "A signed OHOS GUI test bundle reaches the target, base tests pass, but GUI geometry/focus or graphics-context cases fail or crash under a non-native browser backend."
phenomenon: "A signed target test can report a successful case with zero assertions when a capability patch returns unconditionally; marker text may also be absent from an audit allow-list or end with a literal backslash-n."
root_cause: "Browser rendering alone does not imply native window, key-state, or graphics-context support. Geometry may instead fail because parent client allocation is incomplete. A Drawing crash with non-null renderer occurred in executable-path-based reference discovery, not context creation; an explicit fixture root exposed a missing upstream basic-case golden file. Unconditional returns hide missing assertions; console and GUI inventories differ."
resolution: "Correct parent client allocation with bounded paint wait, retaining clipping assertions. Respect the selected native art provider size hint, bind explicit help-event origin and activation, and bind official fixture-root inputs to the signed child sandbox. When a portable image is independently specified but its upstream golden is absent, assert exact dimensions, pixels and transparency; never generate a golden from target output or widen tolerance. Derive marker ownership from actual XML TestCase ancestors, keep console and GUI inventories separate, and use root assertion totals: absent per-case counts remain unknown rather than inferred zero from Section aggregates."
verification: "Fresh formal USB transaction wxwidgets-3332-review-usb-r37 bound 22 production patches and all 19 touched source files to native build inputs; signed HAP SHA256 fb3ce579e5a3b39f5fa96e4efc0f02460c5d70be749738a649cc6ce36ed6ddaf, unique launch=1, complete hash-linked receipts through POSTRELEASE_PASS. Base429/GUI467/Drawing1 executed with zero failed assertions; assertion totals1161894/32916/4. GUI/Drawing have zero capability markers; Base has33 marked cases/40 explained branch events. Consumer1/1, state3/3 and graceful wxEntry RC0 passed. Task-specific acceptance of explained limits does not prove skipped branches or a native OHOS window backend. Historical r24/r30-r35 results remain separate."
scope: "Applies to signed HAP validation of GUI libraries using Broadway or other browser-backed surfaces on OHOS PC."
safety: "Do not treat process RC 0, Catch success=true, or N/N case completion alone as functional PASS when assertions are zero or markers are unaudited. Never splice shell-domain and app-domain results or rerun a consumed launch."
evidence: "F:/HarmonyPC/wxwidgets-333/review-w3-r37/usb-freeze.json; F:/HarmonyPC/wxwidgets-333/review-w3-r37/usb-result-frozen.json; F:/HarmonyPC/wxwidgets-333/review-submit-r36/candidate-source-binding-r2.json"
